The '''2017 UEFA Super Cup''' was the 42nd edition of the [[UEFA Super Cup]], an annual [[association football|football]] match organised by [[UEFA]] and contested by the reigning champions of the two main [[Europe]]an club competitions, the [[UEFA Champions League]] and the [[UEFA Europa League]]. The match featured [[Royal Spanish Football Federation|Spanish]] side [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]], the title holders and winners of the [[2016–17 UEFA Champions League]], and [[The Football Association|English]] side [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]], the winners of the [[2016–17 UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0250-0c5117033ac2-e4519dd2909f-1000--real-madrid-to-face-manchester-united-in-super-cup/|title=Real Madrid to face Manchester United in Super Cup|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |website=[[UEFA]]|date=3 June 2017}}</ref> The match was played at the [[Toše Proeski Arena|Philip II Arena]] in [[Skopje]], [[North Macedonia|FYR Macedonia]], on 8 August 2017, and was the first UEFA final staged in the country.<ref name="host">{{cite news|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0250-0c510bc25a1e-a6363aff6bb8-1000--fyr-macedonia-to-host-2017-uefa-super-cup/|title=FYR Macedonia to host 2017 UEFA Super Cup|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |website=[[UEFA]]|date=30 June 2015}}</ref>

Real Madrid won the match 2–1 for their second consecutive and fourth overall UEFA Super Cup title.<ref name="bbc"/>

